.TH UPLAY 1 "October 2026" "uplay 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
uplay \- lightweight, Linux-first music player and engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B uplay
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fITARGET\fR]
.br
.B uplay
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBuplay\fR is a fast, terminal-first music player built for Linux following the Unix philosophy.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-shuffle\fR
Enable shuffle playback mode.
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-repeat\fR \fIMODE\fR
Set repeat mode (off, one, playlist).
.TP
\fB\-\-resume\fR
Resume playback from previous session.
.TP
\fB\-\-stdin\fR
Read audio paths from standard input.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose debug output.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBplay\fR [\fITARGET\fR]
Play target file/directory or resume playback.
.TP
\fBpause\fR
Pause active playback.
.TP
\fBstop\fR
Stop playback.
.TP
\fBnext\fR
Advance to next track.
.TP
\fBprevious\fR
Return to previous track.
.TP
\fBvolume\fR \fILEVEL\fR
Set volume level (0..=100).
.TP
\fBqueue\fR \fITARGET\fR
Enqueue track or URL.
.SH AUTHORS
UPlay Contributors.
